gal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Battles will enter with double the normal number of defense counters.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Doubling Season affects permanents that enter with counters.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Everything that is specified by the effect creating the original token or tokens will also be true about the additional token or tokens created by Doubling Season's replacement effect. For example, if an effect tells you to create a token \"tapped and attacking,\" the additional tokens will also be tapped and attacking.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If there are two Doubling Seasons on the battlefield, then the number of tokens or counters is four times the original number. If there are three on the battlefield, then the number of tokens or counters is eight times the original number, and so on.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Planeswalkers will enter with double the normal number of loyalty counters. However, if you activate an ability whose cost has you put loyalty counters on a planeswalker, the number you put on isn't doubled. This is because those counters are put on as a cost, not as an effect.","oracle_id":"01546b7d-a233-4176-8843-d732074dc5b6","published_at":"2024-11-08","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The creature that’s targeted by Arcbound Fiend’s middle ability doesn’t have to have any +1/+1 counters on it. If it doesn’t have a counter on it when the ability resolves, nothing happens.","oracle_id":"72e6cc74-0574-4421-a6b8-97d180484950","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If this creature gets enough -1/-1 counters put on it to cause its toughness to be 0 or less (or the damage marked on it to be lethal), modular will put a number of +1/+1 counters on the target artifact creature equal to the number of +1/+1 counters on this creature before it left the battlefield.","oracle_id":"72e6cc74-0574-4421-a6b8-97d180484950","published_at":"2006-09-25","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The +1/+1 counter is moved only if both targets are still legal as the ability resolves.","oracle_id":"7b303881-ac8d-4459-b04e-768a6804763c","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The two targets of the last ability must be different creatures. Either one may be Daghatar the Adamant.","oracle_id":"7b303881-ac8d-4459-b04e-768a6804763c","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To move a counter from one creature to another, the counter is removed from the first creature and placed on the second. Any abilities that care about a counter being placed on the second creature will apply.","oracle_id":"7b303881-ac8d-4459-b04e-768a6804763c","published_at":"2014-11-24","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Each additional Hardened Scales you control will increase the number of +1/+1 counters placed on a creature you control by one.","oracle_id":"a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature you control would enter the battlefield with a number of +1/+1 counters on it, it enters with that many plus one instead.","oracle_id":"a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If two or more effects attempt to modify how many counters would be put on a creature you control, you choose the order to apply those effects, no matter who controls the sources of those effects.","oracle_id":"a1f3da21-af6d-450e-bf0b-985d158418e6","published_at":"2023-09-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
